# Half-Life .357 revolver (Colt Python). Measured by vrcardgen, finished by
# hand.
#
# The cylinder is bone "revolver", swinging 1.100 radians - 63 degrees -
# about Y in `reload`. That is the whole mechanism a hand needs: open it,
# tip the muzzle up and the cases fall out, fill it, close it, shoot.
#
# The model also has six SHELL bones and a speed_loader that travel in from
# off-screen during the reload. Those are ROUNDS, not joints, and the feed
# path owns them - a card declaring six hinges would have the simulator
# trying to drive the ejecting brass.
#
# NOT declared, deliberately:
#   trigger  - it moves 0.754 rad in `fire1`, but it is driven by the analog
#              trigger and the sear, not by a hand grabbing it. Left to the
#              existing path so it keeps animating.
#   hammer   - exists, owns 2.6% of the mesh, and is never animated in any
#              sequence. Single-action thumbing needs a travel stated by
#              hand, which nobody has measured yet.

weapon v_357
match  bones 44  seqs 8  hash 0xba7f43f7

type   revolver  capacity 6  rpm 300

joint 0  bone "revolver"  hinge  travel 1.10  rest 0
    grab  point 0.00 0.00 0.00  radius 3.0
